# Figma button chrome — Mobile NP PDP SoT (non-negotiable)

> **Web** Share/Save is a different recipe (42×42 + `border/default`) — see `figma-np-pdp-web-ui.mdc` / `3422:4581`.  
> **Mweb NP PLOT handcraft (`FINALL`)** gallery chrome: 40×40, `radius/m`, stroke **`border/subtle` 1.5**, Back fill `surface/subtle` — see `figma-mweb-np-plot-ui`. This file is mobile chrome baseline; FINALL wins when replicating that SoT.

## Source of truth (in order — do not skip)

1. **Approved Figma frame:** `Mobile / NP PDP / First fold` (`4678:13581`) on page **PDP** in Demand Component Kit  
2. **Builder that created it:** `scratch/figma-mobile-np-pdp-first-fold.mjs` (`iconBtn` → `bindRadiusAll(..., radiusM)`)  
3. Bricks tokens only (`radius/*`, `surface/*`, `border/*`, `icon/*`)

**If (1) and a CSS file disagree → Figma first fold wins.**  
**Never** “improve” chrome from `pdp-mobile.css`, Housing.com live, web NP PDP, or generic iOS circle habits.

## Hard ban — do not bypass

- **Do not** set Back / Share / Save to `radius/full` or `border-radius: 50%` / circular chips.  
- **Do not** invent a new chrome recipe because another file looks rounder.  
- **Do not** rewrite `figma-button-chrome` recipes from memory mid-task without re-measuring `4678:13581`.  
- **Do not** apply a “fix” that changes radius/fill/stroke on icon chrome unless the user asked **and** you re-diff against the first-fold SoT.

Bypassing this (e.g. switching `radius/m` → `radius/full` to match CSS) is a **regression**.

## Recipe A — Media / gallery icon chrome (Back / Share / Save)

User-locked mobile gallery recipe (overrides older SoT “stroke none”):

| Prop | Required |
|---|---|
| Size | **40×40** FIXED / FIXED |
| Fill | `surface/white` |
| Radius | **`radius/m` (12)** — rounded square, **not** circle |
| Stroke | **`border/default` · weight `1.5`** · align INSIDE |
| Icon | Iconography — Bricks; color `icon/grey_1` |
| Align | CENTER / CENTER |

**Hard ban:** Do not drop gallery icon stroke to 0 / 1px — mobile gallery icons are **1.5px**.

